<title>UK: UK monetary committee decisions by majority - Brown.</title>
<headline>UK monetary committee decisions by majority - Brown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchquer Gordon Brown said on Tuesday that policy decisions by a new British monetary committee would be taken by majority vote.</p>
<p>&quot;The decisions will be made by a vote of the committee with each member having one vote. If there is no majority, the Governor will have the final vote. The Treasury will have the right to be represented in a non-voting capacity,&quot; Brown said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
